  "projectUrl": "https://vegarise.com/Products/VDocs",
  "published": "2026-02-27T22:35:53.493Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "📦 VDocs – Release Notes\n🚀 Version: 2026.3.1\n\n🔧 Table DOM Enhancements\n\n✨ New Features\n\n📊 Data-Driven Table Creation\n\nAdded new factory methods to simplify table generation from common data sources:\n\n - Table.FromDataTable(...)\n\n - Table.FromCsv(string filePath, ...)\n\n - Table.FromCsv(Stream stream, ...)\n\n - Table.FromEnumerable(...)\n\n - Table.FromStrings(...)\n\nThese APIs allow developers to generate fully populated tables directly from:\n\n - DataTable\n\n - CSV files or streams\n\n - Generic collections (IEnumerable)\n\n - Simple string collections\n\nThis significantly reduces boilerplate code when building reports or exporting structured data.\n\n📈 Developer Experience\n\n - Strongly-typed, discoverable APIs\n\n - Consistent behavior across all data-source factory methods\n\n - Simplified reporting and export scenarios\n\n - Reduced manual row/cell construction logic\n\n 🛠 Stability\n\n - No breaking changes to existing Table APIs\n\n - Backward compatible with previous versions\n\n - Safe to upgrade\n\n🎯 Why This Matters\n\n - Generating tables for reports, exports, and document automation is now:\n\n - Faster to implement\n\n - Cleaner in code\n\n - More consistent\n\n - Less error-prone",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
  "title": "VDocs - Word Document Framework",
  "verbatimVersion": "2026.3.1",
